{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 29, :comments ["<b>Not.</b> The Gaon [Saadia] says: this is for a sign — when you see that you have multiplied, then the seven nations will be cut off, and there is no need [for this explanation]. For he stated the reason why He would not drive them out in one year, namely lest the land become desolate, for the land of Israel will be very long [vast] and those who came out of Egypt will not be able to settle all of it, like lest it be forfeited (Deuteronomy 22:9)."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {0 "Resolved הגאון as the Gaon [Saadia] per standard convention. The phrase ואין צורך appears to be Ibn Ezra's dismissal of Saadia's reading; translated without expanding."}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:37:52.647043996Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}